$ python3 experiments.py --only sandwich_fprime
f'(v) = dm(v, m), m = K turned over, K uniform secret key deck, C36.  Test: query y1 = f'(h) at uniform h; W := (h^-1 * y1) * h^-1; query y2 = f'(h2), h2 = h with two random edge orientations flipped; accept iff y2 == h2 * W * h2.
real f' (100000 games, fresh key each, 10 chunks, seeds 2026+c): accepted 5105/100000 = 0.0510, 95% CI (Wilson) [0.0497,0.0524]
  accepted == (W unchanged by the flip) in every game; W unchanged 5105/100000
  both flipped edges unread by query 1's block: 4772/100000 = 0.0477; all of these accepted (4772); accepted with a flipped edge read: 333/100000 = 0.0033
random-function control (100000 games, seeds 2026+1000+c; query 2 answered by a fresh uniform position): accepted 0/100000, 95% upper bound 3.0e-05 (=1/33,381)
  exact ideal rate: 1/|G| = 2^-225.90 (|G| = 1.0067e+68); advantage = 0.0510 - 2^-225.9
per key (100 keys x 200 tests, seeds 2026+2000+c): accept rate min 0.010, median 0.055, max 0.095, mean 0.0509; variance / binomial variance = 0.85
